  "bodyTypst": "Let $f$ and $g$ be the functions given by $f(x)= e^(x)$ and $g(x)= ln x$.\n\n(a) Find the area of the region enclosed by the graphs of $f$ and $g$ between $x = frac(1,2)$ and $x = 1$.\n\n(b) Find the volume of the solid generated when the region enclosed by the graphs of $f$ and $g$ between $x = frac(1,2)$ and $x = 1$ is revolved about the line $y = 4$.\n\n(c) Let $h$ be the function given by $h(x)= f(x)- g(x)$. Find the absolute minimum value of $h(x)$ on the closed interval $frac(1,2) <= x <= 1$, and find the absolute maximum value of $h(x)$ on the closed interval $frac(1,2) <= x <= 1$. Show the analysis that leads to your answers.",
